    "method": [
      "Soil mask: flood fill from (160,170) over opaque ground pixels with r>g+18, r>b+25, g<170; grass, fence and sky stay outside.",
      "Troughs: per 4px column, luminance (0.3R+0.59G+0.11B) averaged over x+-3 inside the mask and smoothed over y+-2; local minima darker than 72 within +-7px are trough samples, linked across columns from seeds x=14..302, then least-squares lines y=a+bx (n>=12 samples, rms<2px, duplicates within 5px at x=160 merged).",
      "Row vanishing point: weighted least-squares intersection of the eight trough lines (weight = sample count).",
      "Left field side: least-squares line through the soil mask top boundary for x=4..222 (upper-left grass/soil edge). Far edge: same for x=236..318.",
      "Column vanishing point: the trough lines intersect the left side at x_k; x_k=(A+Bk)/(1+Ck) fitted by linear least squares (max residual 0.95px); its limit B/C on the left side is the column vanishing point, so trough spacing and column convergence come from one projective map.",
      "Homography p(u,v) ~ depthPerUnit*u*rowVP + depthPerUnit*v*columnVP + origin (homogeneous, origin = trough 0 on the left side). v=k is trough k, v=k+0.5 is the ridge crest between troughs; u is measured along the ridges from the left side (u=0).",
      "Field bounds in (u,v): medians of the soil-mask boundary mapped through the inverse homography: left side top boundary x=4..222, far edge x=236..318, near edge bottom boundary x=0..150, right side = rightmost soil pixel for y=205..292 (lower-right grass edge).",
      "Soil outline: the soil mask with enclosed stone/shadow holes filled; top = first soil pixel per x, bottom = first pair of non-soil pixels below it (y>=150), sampled every 8px after a +-4px conservative max/min filter. Roots must stay marginPx inside top/bottom; the x=0 and x=320 frame sides are not field edges."
    ],
